---
// Advisor Disclosure & Privacy statement — wording is the client's, verbatim, from
// "Website notes.docx" (brand/content-revision/, 2026-10-17). Don't edit the copy
// without client sign-off; it's a regulatory document.
//
// The draft's bracketed analytics sentence ("If you use analytics or cookies…")
// was removed per its own instruction, since no analytics/cookies are installed
// yet. When GA4 / Vercel Analytics go in, add a sentence under "Information
// collected through this website" naming them.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { office, telHref } from '../data/site';

const carriers = [
	'BMO Insurance',
	'Beneva',
	'Canada Life',
	'Empire Life',
	'Foresters Financial',
	'iA Financial Group (Industrial Alliance)',
	'Manulife',
	'RBC Insurance',
	'Sun Life',
	'The Edge Benefits',
];
---

<Layout
	title="Advisor Disclosure & Privacy"
	description="Who we are, the insurers we work with, how we're paid, and how we protect your personal information."
>
	<section class="bg-enterprise-blue-500">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-24">
			<h1 data-reveal class="text-4xl leading-tight font-semibold text-white md:text-5xl">Advisor Disclosure & Privacy</h1>
		</div>
	</section>

	<article class="legal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 text-natural-grey-800">
		<h2>Who we are</h2>
		<p>
			Enterprise Life Insurance & Investment Solutions Inc. is an independent insurance brokerage based in Pickering,
			Ontario. Our advisors are licensed as life insurance agents by the Financial Services Regulatory Authority of
			Ontario (FSRA).
		</p>

		<h2>The companies we work with</h2>
		<p>
			Because we're independent, we're not tied to a single insurer. We hold contracts with, and can recommend products
			from, the following companies:
		</p>
		<p class="font-medium text-natural-grey-900">{carriers.join(' · ')}</p>
		<p>
			We work with these insurers through HUB Financial Inc., a Managing General Agency that provides administrative and
			contracting support between brokers and insurance companies.
		</p>
		<p>No insurance company owns any part of our business, and we hold no ownership interest in any insurance company.</p>

		<h2>How we're paid</h2>
		<p>
			You don't pay us a fee for insurance advice. When you buy a policy through us, the insurance company pays us a
			commission. If you keep the policy in force, we may also receive ongoing renewal or service commissions.
		</p>
		<p>
			From time to time, insurers may also offer additional compensation, such as bonuses or non-monetary incentives,
			based on factors like the volume of business placed or how long policies stay in force. We're happy to explain how
			we'll be paid on any product we recommend. Just ask.
		</p>

		<h2>Investment products</h2>
		<p>
			We offer segregated fund contracts, which are investment products issued by life insurance companies. They can be
			held in non-registered accounts and in registered plans such as RRSPs and TFSAs. Segregated funds are offered under
			our life insurance licences, through the insurers we're contracted with, and are placed through HUB Financial Inc.
		</p>
		<p>
			Segregated fund contracts include features such as maturity and death benefit guarantees and the ability to name a
			beneficiary. The terms of these guarantees vary by contract.
		</p>
		<p>
			Segregated fund policies are issued by the insurance company. Any amount allocated to a segregated fund is invested
			at the risk of the contractholder and may increase or decrease in value.
		</p>

		<h2>Conflicts of interest</h2>
		<p>
			We take potential conflicts of interest seriously. If we become aware of a conflict that could affect a
			recommendation we make to you, we'll tell you. Our recommendations are always based on our analysis of your
			financial security needs.
		</p>

		<h2>Your privacy</h2>
		<p>
			We comply with the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA) and applicable Ontario
			privacy laws.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>What we collect and why.</strong> To give you advice and apply for coverage on your behalf, we collect personal,
			financial and health information. We collect only what we need to recommend suitable products, complete your
			application and service your policies.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Who we share it with.</strong> With your consent, we share your information with the insurers you apply to and
			with our Managing General Agency, HUB Financial Inc., in order to place and service your coverage. With your
			permission, we may also involve trusted associates when you need help outside our area of expertise. We never sell
			your personal information.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Your consent.</strong> We ask for your written consent before collecting and sharing your information as part
			of an application. You may withdraw consent at any time. Because we can't advise you or service your coverage
			without this information, withdrawing consent may end our working relationship.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>How we protect it.</strong> Paper records are kept in secure, locked storage. Electronic files are
			password-protected and encrypted. Records we no longer need are securely shredded or destroyed. Everyone on our team
			understands the sensitivity of client information and their obligation to protect it.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Keeping it accurate.</strong> We rely on accurate information to give good advice. You may ask to review the
			information we hold about you at any time and request corrections. We'll also update it as your circumstances change.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>How long we keep it.</strong> We keep your information for as long as you're our client, and afterward as long
			as we have a legal or business need to retain it.
		</p>

		<h2>Information collected through this website</h2>
		<p>
			When you contact us through this website, we collect the information you provide, such as your name, email, phone
			number and message, and use it only to respond to your inquiry.
		</p>

		<h2>Communicating electronically</h2>
		<p>
			With your consent, we may communicate with you by email and other electronic means. You can withdraw that consent at
			any time.
		</p>

		<h2>Questions or concerns</h2>
		<p>
			Our Privacy Officer is Jay Bablani. To review your information, ask a question or raise a concern, contact:
		</p>
		<address class="not-italic">
			{office.name}<br />
			Attn: Jay Bablani, Privacy Officer<br />
			{office.street}<br />
			{office.city}<br />
			<a href={telHref(office.phone)}>{office.phone}</a> ·
			<a href="mailto:jay.bablani@enterpriselife.ca">jay.bablani@enterpriselife.ca</a>
		</address>
		<p>
			We'll look into any complaint and respond as soon as practical. If you're not satisfied with our response, you may
			contact the <a href="https://www.olhi.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OmbudService for Life & Health Insurance (OLHI)</a>
			or <a href="https://www.fsrao.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FSRA</a>. For more about PIPEDA, visit the Office of the
			Privacy Commissioner of Canada at <a href="https://www.priv.gc.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">priv.gc.ca</a>.
		</p>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.legal h2 {
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--color-natural-grey-900);
	}

	.legal h2:first-child {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.legal p,
	.legal address {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.legal strong {
		color: var(--color-natural-grey-900);
	}

	.legal a {
		color: var(--color-enterprise-blue-500);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>
